  introduced:['Sally Sin (new character introduced)'],
  sum:'After the battle at Booyeong, Chad walks away with a cold heart. Jade\'s trust is shaken, and the words she spoke still echo in his mind; he has lost something precious and does not know how to fix it. In a lantern-lit brothel at the edge of the city, a woman named Sally welcomes guests. Behind the smile lies the story of a fallen princess and a heart that never forgot its wounds. Once she was a princess of a noble house; she believed in love and trusted the man at her side, but it was a lie: he used her, betrayed her and brought down her family for power. Her home fell, her family was gone and she became a fugitive with no name and no land. Now she lives as Sally in a brothel, not as a prostitute but as a woman who waits: she endures, she listens, she gathers information, all for the day she can take her revenge. That night a broken man comes to her: "You look as if the world has betrayed you too." "...Maybe it has." "You don\'t have to pretend here. Everyone who comes to me carries a wound." She understands him because she too lost everything once. For that night Chad sets aside his pain and finds warmth in her presence; she does not ask about his past. Banners: New Character Introduced: Sally Sin. Sally + Chad Bond: Forming.',
